      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shift toward \"industrial independence\" is a double-edged sword that offers short-term security against supply chain shocks but often comes at the cost of long-term economic efficiency and innovation. While it protects vulnerable domestic sectors, it can also lead to higher prices for consumers and slow the global adoption of necessary technologies if nations pursue fragmented, non-standardized paths. Ultimately, its success depends on whether countries can balance defensive protectionism with the need to remain deeply integrated in global markets to access capital and expertise.",
      "source": "target",
